in the kernel.  The default is to make everything static,  unless
some reason requires the opposite.  There are several reasons for
this  policy,  the  main one is that the kernel is one monolithic
name‐space, and pollution is not a good idea  here  either.   For
device  drivers and other modules that don’t add new internal in‐
terfaces to the kernel, the entire source should be in  one  file
if  possible.   That  way all symbols can be made static.  If for
some reason a module is split over multiple  source  files,  then
